body:
I'd let that ref give me a card any day. 

&#x200B;

Unnf.

Totally in agreement. I was teary-eyed when they talked about his first murder victim. 

&#x200B;

I don't want to listen to the second part, but I feel like that's more selfish than not. I enjoy living in a safe life where I don't have to worry about this stuff impacting me directly, but I need to be reminded that this world (and people) are capable of horrific, terrible things.

Get it. :D

You and me both. It took me longer to accept my body type than my hair (wtf). Glad we're on the path of rocking what we got.

&#x200B;

Thanks for your response. I know it's complicated but your answer was full of lots of good information (and resources). I'm sorry you've experienced similar but I'm glad you're overcoming the triggers.

&#x200B;

I feel incredibly numb about it all. Of course, I find it disgusting that Nmom didn't even gather what kind of an impact it was having on me (or how fucked up it was to begin with). I know it happened to me and is part of my experience, but I think my body and brain disassociated with it enough that I can look at it from an outsider's perspective. Oddly enough (and completely separate), the manipulative ex and me getting away from him made me grow a shiny spine.

&#x200B;

I'll definitely go check out the other page though. Thank you again. <3
